  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1221 PM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nTonight through Saturday...Isolated rain chances will continue \nacross southeastern portions of the area this afternoon as the \ncut-off low moves across the Gulf coastline. After sunset, \nclear/quiet conditions are expected this evening as rain chances \ndiminish across I-59 and HWY 84 corridor. Patchy fog may be \npossible early Monday morning. \n\nHigh pressure will settle over the Southeast CONUS over the course \nof this week, lingering through the rest of the week. Dangerous heat \nconcerns are expected to return as highs range in the mid/upper 90s \nand heat indices reach 105-110F. Areawide \"Limited\" heat risk will \ncontinue to be advertised and more than like extend into the week. \nWe will also monitor for any need for heat advisories on a day-to-\nday basics. As the high settles, additional cut-off low disturbances \nwill traverse around the ridge, bringing deep moisture and storm \nchances (25-50%) starting along the HWY 84 corridor. Mid-week, rain \nchances will expand to the I-20 corridor and eastern MS as the \npattern lingers into the end of the week. /SW/",
